Experiment 8: Dynamic Memory Allocation in C

Steps:
Open the Ubuntu terminal.
Create the C program using nano expt8.c.
Write the C program for dynamic memory allocation using malloc() and signal handling.
Save the file using Ctrl + O, press Enter, and exit using Ctrl + X.
Compile the program using gcc expt8.c -o expt8.
Execute the program using ./expt8 100.
Observe the memory allocation success message.
Press Ctrl + C to generate an interrupt and release the allocated memory.
Check memory usage using free -h.
Check the process using ps aux | grep expt8.
Execute free -h again to observe memory usage after termination.
Result: Dynamic memory allocation and deallocation were performed successfully using malloc(), free(), and signal handling.
